title: Distro Gallery

files:
  - .assets/img-103-09-01.png
  - .assets/img-103-09-02.png
  - .assets/img-103-09-03.png

steps:
  - cmds:
      - view 1
    text: |
      {[ht,$start]&thinsp;Distro Gallery}

      The last handful of tours examined the details of (MCU-specific) content supplied by our `rpi.2040` distro {[dc,R]}.

      This tour takes a bird's-eye view of those sources &ndash; plac&shy;ing files from {[dc,R]} next to counterparts from distros {[dc,N]} and {[dc,T]}.

      We'll use capitalized markers [{[bm,A]}&thinsp;] to highlight com&shy;mon elements to aid viewing source files side-by-side.

      We'll then numeric circles [&thinsp;{[dc,1]}&thinsp;] to highlight additional details within these files as needed.

      <div class="em-info">

      **VS Code**💡&ndash; hide the **Primary Sidebar** and **Bottom Panel** to best view _code triptych_ series that follows.

      </div>

  - cmds:
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,photo]&thinsp;%[cu]BuildC%}

      Recalling its special relationshp with the **EMS** translator, {[cu]BuildC}&thinsp;{[tr,103/03/01]} provides an entry-point into any distro.

      We've peeked earlier at {[cs]em$configure} in these files, not&shy;ing _commonality_ in declaring MCU interrupts {[tr,103/06/04]}.

      Synthesis of `build.sh` and `load.sh` scripts within their {[cs]em$generate} implementations follows suit:

      {[BM,A]} specification of the MCU's memory map<br>
      {[BM,B]} compiler flags reflecting the CPU's architecture<br>
      {[BM,C]} a platform-specific command for loading executables<br>

      {[DC,1]} a repeatable pattern for any MCU with **JLink** support

      <div class="em-info">

      A future utility might synthesize `build.sh` fragments for these (and other) distros using **Segger** compilers.

      </div>

  - cmds:
      - view 3
    text: |
      {[ht,photo]&thinsp;%[cu]BoardC%}

      Having made _many_ stops at the `rpi.2040` {[dc,R]} {[cu]BoardC}, we see almost identical code in its distro {[dc,N]}&thinsp;&middot;&thinsp;{[dc,T]} counterparts.

      Some details about their {[cs]em$configure} implementations:

      {[BM,A]} per-board bindings of logical pin names<br>
      {[BM,B]} assigning a (MCU-specific) scalar for {[cu]BusyWait}<br>

      {[DC,1]} set {[cn]MHZ_P} [=&thinsp;48] to match the MCU system clock<br>
      {[DC,2]} disable on-board SPI flash to save power<br>

      Similar to a top-level HW module in VHDL/Verilog, {[cu]BoardC} serves as a "collection" point for distro content.

      <div class="em-info">

      Yes, we shamelessly "cut-copy-paste" proven {[cu]BoardC} implementations when fielding a new distro.

      </div>

